@JakobDegen 

> Type checking main will just require lowering the generator for the async block inside it, which seems fine. Of course someone could try to make an actual cycle (via mutual recursion or something) but that's already unsupported.

Async blocks and closures are type-checked together with their enclosing function, and there can be dependencies between them for type-inference purposes. 

Example:

```rust
fn foo() {
    let v: Vec<_> = vec![];
    let x = async {
        v.push(22);
    };
    ...
}
```

