> Could `#[derive(Debug)]` put a `T: Copy` assertion in the generated code instead of requiring the derive to be present?

Ah, you already had this idea (https://github.com/retep998/winapi-rs/issues/1030#issuecomment-1364755365).

Perhaps this could be implemented by calling a function which requires the struct to be `Copy`.

```
impl fmt::Debug for UnitStruct {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter) -> fmt::Result {
        fn ensure_copy<T: Copy>(_: &T) {}
        ensure_copy(self);
        // rest of the generated debug impl
    }
}
